1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,960
In Boston,

2
00:00:01,040 --> 00:00:02,400
sugary syrup was leaking

3
00:00:02,480 --> 00:00:04,640
from an enormous storage tank.

4
00:00:04,720 --> 00:00:06,000
Children came with buckets

5
00:00:06,040 --> 00:00:07,840
to collect it around the base.

6
00:00:08,080 --> 00:00:08,320
Residents

7
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:09,680
complained about the leaks,

8
00:00:09,760 --> 00:00:10,960
but the company had its own

9
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:12,880
solution: it painted the tank

10
00:00:12,960 --> 00:00:13,680
brown to make

11
00:00:13,760 --> 00:00:15,520
the streaks less noticeable.

12
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:17,760
The tank remained in use.

13
00:00:17,840 --> 00:00:19,280
The fifteen-meter-tall steel

14
00:00:19,440 --> 00:00:21,040
tank stood beside a dock,

15
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:22,960
close to residential buildings.

16
00:00:23,040 --> 00:00:24,320
It held molasses,

17
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:25,440
a thick syrup left

18
00:00:25,520 --> 00:00:27,280
over from sugar production.

19
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:28,880
Ships delivered the molasses,

20
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:30,000
which was then sent away

21
00:00:30,080 --> 00:00:31,920
to be turned into alcohol.

22
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:33,280
In one of the nearby houses

23
00:00:33,360 --> 00:00:34,720
lived Martin Clougherty,

24
00:00:34,840 --> 00:00:36,160
along with his sister Teresa

25
00:00:36,240 --> 00:00:37,760
and their mother Bridget.

26
00:00:37,840 --> 00:00:40,400
On January 15, 1919,

27
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:41,760
the tank contained nearly

28
00:00:41,840 --> 00:00:43,840
nine million liters of molasses.

29
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:45,360
That afternoon,

30
00:00:45,440 --> 00:00:47,280
a tremendous crash rang out.

31
00:00:47,760 --> 00:00:48,880
The tank walls burst

32
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:50,320
apart, and molasses

33
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:51,520
poured into the streets.

34
00:00:52,080 --> 00:00:53,360
The rushing wave tore

35
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:55,040
houses from their foundations,

36
00:00:55,120 --> 00:00:55,520
smashed

37
00:00:55,600 --> 00:00:56,720
the supports of the elevated

38
00:00:56,800 --> 00:00:58,400
railway, and carried wreckage

39
00:00:58,560 --> 00:00:59,600
along with it.

40
00:00:59,760 --> 00:01:00,480
People were knocked

41
00:01:00,560 --> 00:01:01,760
off their feet and pinned

42
00:01:01,840 --> 00:01:03,840
beneath collapsing structures.

43
00:01:03,920 --> 00:01:04,880
At that moment,

44
00:01:04,960 --> 00:01:05,840
Martin was asleep

45
00:01:05,880 --> 00:01:07,840
on the third floor of his home.

46
00:01:07,920 --> 00:01:09,120
The wave tore the house

47
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:10,160
from its foundations

48
00:01:10,280 --> 00:01:10,880
and smashed

49
00:01:10,920 --> 00:01:11,840
it against the elevated

50
00:01:11,960 --> 00:01:13,280
railway structure.

51
00:01:13,360 --> 00:01:13,760
When Martin

52
00:01:13,840 --> 00:01:15,160
regained consciousness,

53
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:17,400
he was surrounded by molasses.

54
00:01:17,440 --> 00:01:18,640
Debris from the destroyed

55
00:01:18,720 --> 00:01:20,440
building had trapped him.

56
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:22,080
He managed to free himself,

57
00:01:22,160 --> 00:01:22,800
pulled his sister

58
00:01:22,880 --> 00:01:23,960
Teresa toward him,

59
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:25,600
and helped her escape.

60
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:26,880
Then Martin began

61
00:01:26,960 --> 00:01:28,533
searching for his mother.

62
00:01:28,587 --> 00:01:28,880
He called

63
00:01:28,960 --> 00:01:30,240
out for her and asked people

64
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:32,120
nearby to help him look.

65
00:01:32,160 --> 00:01:33,440
Later, he was told

66
00:01:33,520 --> 00:01:35,320
that Bridget had died.

67
00:01:35,360 --> 00:01:36,480
Rescuers continued

68
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:37,280
searching for people

69
00:01:37,360 --> 00:01:39,120
among the ruined buildings.

70
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:40,240
The thick molasses made

71
00:01:40,320 --> 00:01:41,680
it difficult to move and clear

72
00:01:41,760 --> 00:01:43,160
away the wreckage.

73
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:43,880
In all,

74
00:01:43,920 --> 00:01:46,600
the disaster killed 21 people.

75
00:01:46,640 --> 00:01:48,320
Around 150 others

76
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:49,480
were injured.

77
00:01:49,520 --> 00:01:51,040
Those affected by the disaster

78
00:01:51,120 --> 00:01:51,760
and the families

79
00:01:51,800 --> 00:01:52,800
of those who died

80
00:01:52,880 --> 00:01:54,160
demanded compensation

81
00:01:54,240 --> 00:01:55,400
from the tank's owner,

82
00:01:55,440 --> 00:01:56,160
United States

83
00:01:56,240 --> 00:01:58,027
Industrial Alcohol.

84
00:01:58,053 --> 00:01:58,720
But the company

85
00:01:58,880 --> 00:02:00,520
denied responsibility.

86
00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:01,040
It claimed

87
00:02:01,120 --> 00:02:02,640
that anarchists had destroyed

88
00:02:02,720 --> 00:02:04,773
the tank by planting a bomb.

89
00:02:04,827 --> 00:02:05,680
The legal proceedings

90
00:02:05,960 --> 00:02:07,960
continued for several years.

91
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:08,320
The court

92
00:02:08,400 --> 00:02:09,600
appointed Hugh Ogden

93
00:02:09,640 --> 00:02:11,160
to examine the case.

94
00:02:11,200 --> 00:02:13,093
In April 1925,

95
00:02:13,147 --> 00:02:15,093
he rejected the bomb theory.

96
00:02:15,147 --> 00:02:16,000
The tank had failed

97
00:02:16,080 --> 00:02:16,800
because of flaws

98
00:02:16,880 --> 00:02:18,107
in its construction,

99
00:02:18,133 --> 00:02:19,440
and the disaster had resulted

100
00:02:19,560 --> 00:02:20,320
from negligence

101
00:02:20,440 --> 00:02:21,520
and poor management.

102
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:22,960
Ogden held United States

103
00:02:23,040 --> 00:02:24,640
Industrial Alcohol fully

104
00:02:24,720 --> 00:02:26,080
responsible for the deaths

105
00:02:26,160 --> 00:02:27,480
and the damage —

106
00:02:27,520 --> 00:02:28,880
the very company that,

107
00:02:29,040 --> 00:02:30,160
before the disaster,

108
00:02:30,240 --> 00:02:31,120
had chosen to hide

109
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:32,720
the signs of leaking molasses

110
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:34,480
beneath a coat of brown paint.

